2025-01-15 Wednesday 22:02:33 ceaug_main.py : INFO  Analyzing the test results and correlating them with the relevant parts of the code can help identify the reasons behind the failures. The errors reported are primarily `NoSuchElementException`, indicating that the Selenium testing framework is unable to locate elements on the web page during the execution of the tests. Below, I'll analyze each failed test and suggest steps to resolve the issues.

### Common Issue Across Tests
The bulk of the test cases are failing due to the web driver not being able to locate elements based on the selectors used. A likely cause for this could be that the application is not fully loaded, or potentially the structure of the HTML could be different than what the test expects. 

### Detailed Analysis of Each Failed Test

